OL,3,GNEWSA'Baby loss leave is welcome, but
OL,4,Amore can be done'
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe founder of a charity says the
OL,7,Fintroduction of leave for more people
OL,8,Fwho experience baby loss is "hugely
OL,9,Fpositive", but believes there is "a
OL,10,Flong way to go" before all losses are
OL,11,Ftreated equally.
OL,13,FSamantha Catanach, from Hull, launched
OL,14,FChasing Rainbows after her own
OL,15,Fexperience of baby loss, to support
OL,16,Fothers dealing with miscarriage,
OL,17,Fstillbirth and infertility.
OL,23,APub: 23-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
